## Build / install / runtime verify

The canonical recipe is in `<docs-hub>/00_shared-rules/verify-build.md`. Quick reference:

```bash
# Build (Gradle wrapper handles JDK + Android SDK)
./gradlew :app:assembleDebug
# Windows: gradlew.bat :app:assembleDebug
# verify: https://developer.android.com/studio/build/building-cmdline

# Install to connected device
adb install -r app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
# verify: https://developer.android.com/tools/adb

# Launch
adb shell am start -n {{package}}/.{{main_activity}}

# Runtime log (capture during/after launch)
adb logcat -d AndroidRuntime:E '*:S' > .ai-workspace/diag/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)-${TASK}-log.txt

# Screenshot
adb shell screencap -p > .ai-workspace/screenshots/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)-${TASK}-after.png

# Lint
./gradlew lint
```

## Git identity

This frontend's Dev commits as `{{git_alias}}`. The alias resolves to:

- Name: `{{author_name}}`
- Email: `{{author_email}}`

Run `git as-{{alias}} commit ...` (alias installed by `/sulde-add-team-member`). Plain `git commit` is blocked by the `check_commit_alias.sh` pre-commit hook.

## Branch convention

- Integration branch: `{{integration_branch}}` (typically `develop`)
- Per-task branches: `dev/{{git_alias}}/{slug}` (enforced by `check_branch_format.sh` pre-commit hook)
- Fast-forward merge to integration; delete branch after merge

## Commit message style

- Imperative, ≤50 chars
- No AI traces — pre-commit hook `check_ai_traces.sh` blocks `AI / Claude / GPT / LLM / generated / auto-generated` keywords
- Reads like an engineer's notes-to-self

Examples for Android:

```
fix: handle null player surface on rebind
refactor: extract base class for safe-area inset
feat: home screen tabs reduced to 2
perf: avoid main-thread spike on RecyclerView bind
```

## Pre-commit hooks

This frontend installs `sulde-cc` git pre-commit hooks via `scripts/pre-commit-installer.sh`. They check:
1. branch protection (no direct commits to `main` / `develop`)
2. branch name format (`dev/<alias>/<slug>`)
3. `git as-<alias>` usage (sentinel env var)
4. AI traces in paths + diff

Do not bypass with `--no-verify` unless the user explicitly authorises it.

## Output language

Default: **{{output_language}}** (e.g. English / Chinese / mixed).

## Self-fix boundary recap

When you finish your task and notice a related but out-of-scope problem:

- **Trivial + safe + in your allowlist**: include in the same commit, mention in handoff
- **Anything else**: leave alone, list under "escalation 候选" in the handoff

The full allowlist is in `<docs-hub>/00_shared-rules/self-fix-boundary.md`. Read once per session.

## Diagnostic tools (Android)

For perf / crash / GPU work the canonical tools are:

| Tool | Use case |
|---|---|
| Android Studio Profiler | CPU / memory / energy / network profiling |
| `dumpsys gfxinfo {{package}}` | Frame timing histogram |
| Perfetto / Systrace | Cross-process traces |
| `adb bugreport` | Full system snapshot |
| LeakCanary | Memory leak detection in debug builds |

Capture the relevant tool output into `.ai-workspace/diag/` and reference from the handoff.

